  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_spoon_cb1af7ee3e28331641beb818bf63683381523f7b2876d4f17f2e41551ee0e82b10d">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>wooden spoon | spoon (MNW s.v. lepel) | tin spoon | spoon, made of box-wood | (spoone of alkemie, spones of aulcamyn) alchemy: a substance produced by alchemy; specifically any of various metal alloys made in imitation of gold or resembling it in color, as varieties of brass or latten, sometimes containing arsenic compounds (OED s.v. alchemy 2), especially quote of 1773: J. Buchanan in J. Milton Paradise Lost (new ed.) 128 (note) Alchemy is a mixture of metals of which spoons, &amp;c. are made | silver spoon | spoon, made of latten</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
